One way to achieve this is by using the 'progress' event. When the video is playing normally, the 'progress' event is fired every time the video data is being read from the source. When the network is buffering, the 'progress' event is not fired. So, by listening to the 'progress' event, we can detect when the video is buffering and resume it.

